# Controls what gets uploaded to Vercel.
#
# vercel.json sets "outputDirectory": "." and its rewrite deliberately excludes
# any path ending in a file extension, so EVERY file in the repo root was being
# served as a static asset. That made the SQL seed scripts (including credential
# hashes), the student import data, the maintenance scripts and the internal
# audit documents publicly downloadable from the live site.
#
# Anything listed here is never uploaded, so it cannot be fetched.

# ── Database scripts: schema, seed data and credential material ──
*.sql

# ── Maintenance / migration scripts — not part of the site ──
*.py
*.cjs
seed_students.js
generate-assets.js

# ── Internal documents ──
*.md
AUDIT_REPORT.html
ChessKidoo_User_Manual.html

# ── Scratch, fixtures and stray dumps ──
scratch/
search_res*.txt
audit-inline.json
schema.json
test_games.pgn

# ── Backend sources: Edge Functions run on Supabase, not Vercel ──
supabase/

# ── Tooling / local config ──
.claude/
node_modules/
package-lock.json

# NOTE: vercel.json itself must stay uploaded — Vercel reads it for the
# rewrites and headers. It contains no secrets.
